00:03:13.094 --> 00:03:18.374
University Day reports that researchers at Cornell and the University of Bristol found

00:03:18.374 --> 00:03:22.114
strong evening side winds and blistering temperatures on one face.

00:03:22.654 --> 00:03:27.174
Infrared data resolve distinct regions instead of averaging light from the whole disk.

00:03:27.714 --> 00:03:31.834
Phase curve measurements tracked how the planets light changed as it circled its star.

00:03:32.394 --> 00:03:36.714
The world is not uniform, with different temperatures and winds from one side to the other.

00:03:37.194 --> 00:03:41.714
This is the first detailed study of an exoplanet with clear atmospheric asymmetry.

00:03:41.714 --> 00:03:45.054
and some hot Jupiters do not behave as even spheres.

