00:04:39.218 --> 00:04:44.423
deeper. Deep and earth mantle, right above the core, a large share of the rock is magnesium

00:04:44.423 --> 00:04:49.583
oxide crystals. They sit under pressure equal to the weight of the whole atmosphere, pressing

00:04:49.583 --> 00:04:55.363
on every square centimeter of surface. Fizz.org reports that on larger rocky worlds called

00:04:55.363 --> 00:05:00.703
super-earth, those same crystals would feel pressures several times higher. That extra

00:05:00.703 --> 00:05:05.423
squeeze can force the material into a new atomic arrangement, or turn it into a liquid

00:05:05.423 --> 00:05:11.503
metal. The change is not gradual. Once pressure crosses a threshold, the crystal lattice collapses

00:05:11.503 --> 00:05:17.363
and the atoms settle into a structure that conducts electricity. Lab work that crushes tiny samples

00:05:17.363 --> 00:05:22.603
between diamond anvils already puts that transition inside the pressure range expected in planets

00:05:22.603 --> 00:05:28.403
only a few times more massive than Earth. A metallic liquid like that could drive magnetic fields

00:05:28.403 --> 00:05:35.023
by dynamal action. Something ordinary magnesium oxide cannot do. The same process may run in the

00:05:35.023 --> 00:05:40.083
cores of gas giants, where magnesium oxide could sit in metallic form even deeper.

00:05:40.683 --> 00:05:45.523
No one yet knows how much of a planet's interior must convert before a global magnetic field

00:05:45.523 --> 00:05:45.883
appears.

00:05:46.483 --> 00:05:51.523
It is also unclear whether the transition builds stable layers that block convection, or

00:05:51.523 --> 00:05:52.523
layers that help it.

00:05:53.143 --> 00:05:58.063
Adams under that crushed shift into arrangements that let electrons move freely, turning an

00:05:58.063 --> 00:05:59.463
insulator into a conductor.

00:06:00.063 --> 00:06:04.283
That is one way some planets could keep strong magnetic fields while others do not.

00:06:04.283 --> 00:06:09.723
Even when size and makeup looks similar from the outside, the exact pressure where magnesium

00:06:09.723 --> 00:06:13.503
oxide turns metallic is still a number models have to pin down.

00:06:14.003 --> 00:06:19.343
Until that threshold is measured under conditions that match real planetary interiors, forecasts

00:06:19.343 --> 00:06:23.383
about which exoplanets host global magnetic shields will stay uncertain.

